---
description: Separate durable repo rules from workflow skills; code and rules before markdown.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Agent context layers

- **`.cursor/rules/`** — Durable repository policy (coding constraints, boundaries). Apply these when writing or reviewing code.
- **`.cursor/skills/`** — Procedural workflows for Cursor and humans; do not assume external tools discover them automatically.
- **`docs/*.md`** — Optional background for people; **never** override what you see in source code. Read **code and tests first** when behavior matters.

If a skill duplicates durable guidance that belongs in rules, mirror only that slice into a rule (avoid 1:1 duplicates).

For active work, prefer pointing collaborators to **relevant source paths** and **`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`** over long doc reading lists.

When a task changes delivery status or execution notes, **`docs/milestones.md`** and **`docs/dev-log.md`** may be updated as a human log; that is not a substitute for verifying behavior in code.
